Currently, I have something that resembles that of a Promise type
extends RefCounted
```gdscript
class_name Promise
signal fired();
var has_fired : bool = false;
var object_listener : Object;
# obj is the object emitting a signal that signifies it is "done"
func _init(obj : Object, signal_name : String):
	object_listener = obj;
	object_listener.connect(signal_name, self._fire);

# padding with empty object parameters so signals don't throw an error
func _fire(a1 = {}, a2 = {}, a3 = {}, a4 = {}, a5 = {}, a6 = {}) -> void:
	has_fired = true;
	emit_signal("fired");

# to evaluate the Promise, await this function call. It will yield until the object has emitted it's signal
# or will immediately continue if it has already emitted.
func evaluate() -> Object:
	if has_fired:
		return object_listener;
	await fired;
	return object_listener;
```
This is obviously not very clean, but an extension to the `await` keyword and creation of a `Promise` type would be more desirable.
